# DomiWEB · design & image sourcing (always)

Never ship a business site that is mostly empty gradient / gray void. Visual design and image sourcing are **required pipeline work**, not optional polish the user must request.

## Before considering a site “done”

1. **Hero must be a full-bleed photographic plane** (Google photo or niche illustrative image). Brand name is the dominant text on that hero.
2. Prefer **real Google `photos` URLs** when usable (https, not example.com / localhost).
3. If Google photos are missing/unusable, **automatically** use `niche.illustrativeImages` from `config/niche.config.json` (files under `public/assets/illustrative/<niche-id>/`).
4. When switching niches, **add/update illustrative assets** for that niche — do not leave `illustrativeImages` empty.
5. Footer honesty:
   - Illustrative only → “Las reseñas provienen de nuestro perfil público de Google · Las fotografías son ilustrativas”
   - Google photos → “Las reseñas y fotografías provienen de nuestro perfil público de Google · Algunas imágenes pueden ser ilustrativas”
6. Mark illustrative shots in UI when used (caption / note). Never imply stock photos are the business’s Google photos.
7. Design bar: expressive system typography, atmosphere, one clear CTA (`tel:` only), mobile-ready, no generic AI purple/cream-terracotta/glow look.
8. Crafted template in `src/generate/site.ts` is the default generator; keep it photographic-first.
9. After site changes: regenerate affected `public/sites/<slug>/`, refresh claim pages if needed, and deploy/push when the user expects live Pages updates.

## Do not

- Ask the user whether they “want images” — assume yes.
- Ship fixture/demo sites without illustrative heroes.
- Invent awards, years, services, or fake testimonials to fill space.
